## Prerequisites

### Software Dependencies

- **vg toolkit** (>= 1.40.0) - Graph-based variant calling
- **samtools** (>= 1.9) - BAM file processing
- **bcftools** (>= 1.9) - Variant calling and processing
- **freebayes** (>= 1.3.0) - Variant calling
- **bgzip/tabix** - VCF compression and indexing
- **qualimap** (optional) - Quality assessment
- **pggb** (for index building) - Pangenome graph builder

### Reference Files

Before running the pipeline, you need to prepare reference files for each genome set:

| Reference Type | FASTA File | Description |
|----------------|------------|-------------|
| 1 genome | `1genomes.fasta` | Single reference genome |
| 3 genomes | `3genomes.fasta` | Three reference genomes |
| 6 genomes | `6genomes.fasta` | Six reference genomes |
| 121 genomes | `LSDV_genomes.fasta` | Full genome collection |

## Installation

1. **Clone the repository:**
```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/lsdv-variant-pipeline.git
cd lsdv-variant-pipeline
```

2. **Make the script executable:**
```bash
chmod +x run.sh
```

3. **Prepare reference indices** (run once per reference type):

```bash
# For 3 genomes
pggb -i 3genomes.fasta -m -S -o LSDV3 -t 36 -p 90 -s 1k -n 3
vg convert -t 12 -g LSDV3.gfa -v > LSDV3.vg
vg convert -x LSDV3.vg > LSDV3.xg
vg convert LSDV3.xg -p > LSDV3.pg
vg autoindex -p LSDV3 -g LSDV3.gfa -t 22
samtools faidx 3genomes.fasta

# Similar commands for 6 and 121 genome sets (see script comments)
```

## Usage

### Basic Usage

```bash
./run.sh <sample_name> [reference_type]
```

**Parameters:**
- `sample_name`: Sample identifier (e.g., SRR11470182)
- `reference_type`: Reference genome set (1, 3, 6, or 121) - defaults to 1

**Examples:**
```bash
# Single genome analysis
./run.sh SRR11470182

# Three genome analysis
./run.sh SRR11470182 3

# Six genome analysis
./run.sh SRR11470182 6

# Full 121 genome analysis
./run.sh SRR11470182 121
```

### SLURM Batch Submission

For processing multiple samples on an HPC cluster:

```bash
# Create sample list file (acc_list.txt)
echo -e "SRR11470182\nSRR10394925\nSRR12345678" > acc_list.txt

# Submit batch jobs for 3-genome analysis
more acc_list.txt | perl -e 'while(<>){ chomp; print "sbatch -c 40 --mem=250G -J $_.job run.sh $_ 3\n" ; }' | bash

# For 121-genome analysis (higher resource requirements)
more acc_list.txt | perl -e 'while(<>){ chomp; print "sbatch -c 50 --mem=450G -J $_.job run.sh $_ 121\n" ; }' | bash
```

### Resource Requirements

| Reference Type | CPUs | Memory | Runtime (est.) |
|----------------|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 genome | 20 | 50G | 2-4 hours |
| 3 genomes | 40 | 250G | 4-8 hours |
| 6 genomes | 40 | 250G | 6-12 hours |
| 121 genomes | 50 | 450G | 12-24 hours |

